RotMatrixX/RotMatrixY: contiguous 15-short matrix temp (scattered-locals)

Both rotate the 3x3 matrix in place: they copy the full 0x1e-byte matrix record into a
stack temp (7 dwords + 1 short) and recompute two rows from it. Ghidra declared only
FRAGMENTS of the temp (X: local_44 dword + 6 shorts; Y: short[6] + 3 shorts) -- the copy
overruns the declared storage and the row reads are layout-dependent. Element mapping is
usage-certain: X reads pairs (t3,t6),(t4,t7),(t5,t8) to rebuild rows 1&2; Y reads t0..t2
and t6..t8 for rows 0&2. This was the LAST unfixed member of the RotMatrix family
(Z fixed in patch 065) and the root of garbage CAR ROTATION MATRICES @0x78a754 -> wheel
world positions with wild z (gte_SetRotMatrix fed junk) -> phantom barrier collisions on
frame 1 -> debris with 170M coords -> negative otz -> the L1 Update_Debris crash chain
(every link watchpoint/asm-proven).

